<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:09:41Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Critics warn of espionage risks as Slovakia restores military-diplomatic representation with Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e3b595bc2a103616a1fc30431b7d935cf4b600c211cfdc017577ecc1d64bf79</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:09:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641--99619951a602.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovakia is restoring military-diplomatic relations with Russia for the first time since 2022. The government has defended the move but critics warn of espionage risks and further damage to trust within NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1eeb00ef310f4467af20831a689593e94337729c6a3f07cb5d2d50f3bc287484</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:09:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>What is holding back Cyprus's Schengen ambitions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a6f71dbd00f35ddcee7b40053a32828bb42d68b257773f806ab25d11a37e87f</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488--5f69812ab764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission says Cyprus is ready to join the Schengen Area. Yet questions relating to the island's division and British military bases could still complicate its path to Europe's border-free travel zone.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Iran 'highly likely' to be behind RAF Fairford incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7420936ea22a80881858a2f6fb1304768e331abb741a1a319cf56dc900d86fe1</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941--7cd1b910595f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham told parliament there were "strong indications" of Iranian involvement. The government summoned Iran's ambassador. The scare at RAF Fairford led to the withdrawal of USAF B-1 heavy bombers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reports arrests of 2 Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with Starlink station fire last month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:220996add2818084a011f4e0a0e855f103ef97f1a2ee1ca8c44d72c92ff44210</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-las/a-79646138--0f2bfafb19a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-last-month/a-79646138?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish authorities have reported the arrests of two Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with alleged sabotage of a Starlink station last month. Prime Minister Donald Tusk called the fire an act of "hybrid warfare."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the Ukrainian 'volunteers' under Russian command?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a172979b8cfe6f4b9514dd045d0f85e1df844b58552d7f55b3337ff84dfec9b8</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555--58ee9f17fd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-ukrainian-volunteers-under-russian-command/a-79629555?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia has announced a battalion consisting of Ukrainian "volunteers." But veterans and former prisoners of war share very different accounts.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump claims Russia and Ukraine agreed to 'energy ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:968991724a55306149dba21afd60bbb3a924d2f842d4c2d7019403bdeaefa892</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T14:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509--966648814544.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-claims-russia-and-ukraine-agreed-to-energy-ceasefire/a-79634509?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says both sides have agreed to stop targeting oil refineries, power plants and other energy infrastructure immediately.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Georgia's surrogacy industry is booming, but at what cost?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a89ee4a42fbbb5fd4dff60b024b2838a1f5d2a147a99dcae603fc645210eaf34</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:09:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/georgia-s-surrogacy-industry-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971--47122bb08522.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/georgia-s-surrogacy-industry-is-booming-but-at-what-cost/a-79629971?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Georgia became a hub for surrogate pregnancies after Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022. DW spoke with parents, and those who wanted to become parents, about the hidden costs of a booming industry.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Schools crisis in France: Investment fails to inspire confidence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aca73b3a6d3b8f70420305ac508cf2f41962162fb53f58e02953cca9478406e2</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T19:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/schools-crisis-in-france-investment-fails-to-inspire-confidence/a-79621916--f1c3b3d7b3e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/schools-crisis-in-france-investment-fails-to-inspire-confidence/a-79621916?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For weeks, schoolchildren in France have been protesting the failing education system. Compared to many other countries, France invests heavily in education but critics say that the funds are not distributed fairly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Macron and Steinmeier struggle to revive Franco-German ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:605ebb6346b02038993f142908191e2a8e3d5e50afaff37b8d6515b9753f67b3</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635--64b747b714b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Presidents Frank-Walter Steinmeier and Emmanuel Macron are about to step down from their offices. Their meeting in France made it clear how urgently the Franco-German partnership needs new momentum.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Lifeline for Ukrainian refugees confronts donor fatigue and online abuse as anti-Ukrainian sentiment grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0d6687eaf2f36f91f8377b18501c4e1bdcb2f6aed7e6a58c4599149318891ab</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-se/a-79613292--19cba8c4d4f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-sentiment-grows/a-79613292?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian woman who fled the war in her country built a lifeline for refugees in Poland. Now her organization faces donor fatigue, funding cuts and rising hostility as support for Ukrainians in Poland wanes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia-Herzegovina will soon have a new grand mufti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8fcc77adc4ea78b7d806146ae8919d286bed457ce9a447c22389a374c1c25fd</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-herzegovina-will-soon-have-a-new-grand-mufti/a-79604402--e3c522fde5e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-herzegovina-will-soon-have-a-new-grand-mufti/a-79604402?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new leader of the Islamic Community in Bosnia-Herzegovina will be elected on October 10. The reis-ul-ulema's role is not only important for Muslims in the country itself, but could inspire Muslims across Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Finland, the world's happiest nation, faces a glum winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15f5cbbd733e1e25b503a69f05baf934d50a12682b7536f0c25d71d311e1ef20</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348--0df829428818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finns have many reasons to feel content, but the country's pile of debt is not one of them. Russia's war in Ukraine has added to the fiscal burden. Can the Nordic nation absorb another shock?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU pulls sponsorship from Disinfo2026 event in Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a4dfd2a0fe958f34fa692e291885863af8c354bb72821304f814cf3fe6b6b6</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615--b060dac4b016.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's diplomatic service, Canada and host nation Lithuania all pulled support from a disinformation event in Vilnius. Amid reports of US pressure, the EU said it was "uncomfortable with the framing" of some panels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Security in the Black Sea region: is Bulgaria the weak link in Europe's defense against threats from Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbee76b7b85358d49d2cded64909c5ad1ca0bf532e19774dcf355a42a5642388</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-/a-79592663--cd93d129d2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-russia/a-79592663?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two ships have sunk off the coast of Bulgaria and Romania after drone attacks in recent days. Bulgaria has held back on pointing the finger at Russia. What does that mean for security in the Black Sea and the region?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea recalls Ukraine ambassador amid POW dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0848b1d7b87c55e5c1b5cc5b5d938c25eee238b2cebd2495c01a617370290d4a</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511--9732a38bcd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has said it will recall its ambassador to Ukraine. Seoul is upset about a transfer of North Korean prisoners of war being made public knowledge at the UN and had demanded — but not received — an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian data centers, could Ukraine soon be offline?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b80f86f563a3c4d9a41c5887f8393c25dcdb7857ed9994ccbcab2606d8106527</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503--ed9380350022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia targets Ukraine's data centers more and more, experts say the country's internet system is too robust to shut down entirely. However, services could become more expensive.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Middle Corridor: Can Bulgaria be a safe gateway for Asian imports to the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1fef6254dc311fdbf4b166f913d93bfad2b3a11513e9f96524d2fa9ae08f339</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530--0deecfdaf02f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants more trade via the Middle Corridor, which could bring big benefits for Bulgaria. But Tuesday's drone attacks on commercial ships off the Bulgarian coast are a stark reminder of the security risks involved.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cc224716cc7a71a3934aca196bf1247df70a93c8c8637d90476485415569149</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: European Commission tables reforms to prepare bloc for new members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aca65614bf042488574e345c9743deb3d0422549a2a8c06b8559f09f6486b936</id><updated>2026-10-13T16:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493--0237e634d1b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission is proposing earlier access to EU markets for candidate countries, new voting rules to reduce vetoes and extra safeguards for a bigger bloc. But is the reform fair — or even feasible?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
